- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}=1).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $4$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we can immediately conclude that \n\n$$\nP({X}^{2}=1)=0.1+0.2=0.3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119941 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ff302ba-5a3f-599b-b038-7417af1dca71" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Tangent Line Using dx/dy"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62979e92-45e9-5dc6-8f39-99cc2e9d96b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{8}-\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245178} {:answer/id #uuid "805e2500-01e2-50d2-a506-5c198597c2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245444} {:answer/id #uuid "844ac3c9-57f1-5fd5-8d04-85a9a8a1b2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{18}-\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245480} {:answer/id #uuid "d811f8f1-2ef1-5c53-a599-574d0712abf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{16}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246237} {:answer/id #uuid "f5245542-2c39-5d0f-b0a9-ba2de27c7518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5245542-2c39-5d0f-b0a9-ba2de27c7518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246476} :answer-field/id #uuid "5234f73d-f7a9-51e5-9340-f6c76b65f21c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246691}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00d18bd8-cfc3-5c89-ac8d-72f20b70464f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110192" :question/problem "Given a curve $x=5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16,$ what is the equation of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(5{y}^{3}-8{y}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{3})-8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{2})+16\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(1) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (3{y}^{2})-8\\cdot (2y)+0 \\\\  & =15{y}^{2}-16y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{15{y}^{2}-16y}.\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $(24,2)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(24,2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15\\cdot {2}^{2}-16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point-slope formula for a tangent line, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-2 & =\\frac{1}{28}(x-24) \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}-\\frac{6}{7}+2 \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{28}+\\frac{8}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064251 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4270c31c-80f1-5b5d-bca8-e16a47206c2b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of an Inverse Function From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19748f7d-bb3c-5578-815a-2c40f268fd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244541} {:answer/id #uuid "245e0993-1c09-56ea-a369-0117d5ee5974" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244637} {:answer/id #uuid "2f2e6757-a78e-5338-abcf-b4cc049dfd1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244738} {:answer/id #uuid "6f36eba8-2e78-54af-916b-61cedc572d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245301} {:answer/id #uuid "721e29cf-a6f9-513b-8aa0-cf84cb7826ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19748f7d-bb3c-5578-815a-2c40f268fd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244541} :answer-field/id #uuid "517e252a-aac0-56a3-81dc-672a79260cc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c68b15f6-2538-56cf-b4b4-1738b9f449cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-110198" :question/problem "![](images/ba/ba762e13c4015b43b99f9038ee63a247584345cd535e12b80c1f3b0d9e50e70b.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a piecewise linear function $y=f(x).$ The point $A$ has coordinates $(1,0)$ and lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $(0,1)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x),$ what is $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $(0,1)$ lies on ${f}^{-1},$ we have ${f}^{-1}(0)=1.$ \nThe slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ for $x\\in [0,2]$ is $-2$, hence, ${f}^{′}(1)=-2.$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse function is \n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18abaef5-2dc8-5961-bd2a-e6cc52cce7bb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Probability Involving a Squared Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96ff421f-9ec2-512a-9157-976daafdff3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397980} {:answer/id #uuid "898e27b7-9ef5-5983-b123-9e3d1e0ea936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397981} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ced49a-d138-52fc-a403-8a1a71eae7fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397982} {:answer/id #uuid "6e6a8fa7-c348-5374-bcae-7fea018ed7b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397983} {:answer/id #uuid "316119b4-ffd0-5c0e-b24d-dbeeefce6b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3ced49a-d138-52fc-a403-8a1a71eae7fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397982} :answer-field/id #uuid "83ad446d-3037-51a4-aa4d-e8f17f3cb63d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "49f435e1-94de-585c-a881-d3c848ebd176" :question/math-academy-id "q-110214" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}=9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first calculate the distribution of ${X}^{2}:$\n\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ | $81$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can immediately conclude that $P({X}^{2}=9)=0.4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247098 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175998 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "18abaef5-2dc8-5961-bd2a-e6cc52cce7bb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Probability Involving a Squared Random Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "279534cc-256e-568c-a937-6ed5b72d8bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244662} {:answer/id #uuid "57c030e1-4016-524a-aca5-c1dfc7fa44d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245089} {:answer/id #uuid "a01b0c6c-4c9b-537a-bd58-deff7249c426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245737} {:answer/id #uuid "a2003abc-a3cf-5ff9-8a42-587cea4e5e4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245757} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb97d52-88c5-516e-8818-9c2adfb64da1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "279534cc-256e-568c-a937-6ed5b72d8bd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244662} :answer-field/id #uuid "337858c6-870c-5a8c-b9cd-fe6c81ad2e09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8d8ecfcd-74a5-52aa-8e4e-67316fa3757f" :question/math-academy-id "q-110220" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}=9).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $9$ | $1$ | $1$ | $9$ | $81$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.35$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we can immediately conclude that \n\n$$\nP({X}^{2}=9)=0.35+0.1=0.45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247108 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064253 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b492068c-2bd2-5611-baab-780959d24c3d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of an Inverse Function Using a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40762dce-3ad8-5bc2-b822-ea828572049b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244877} {:answer/id #uuid "808b95f4-e21b-5dd6-9146-9f4276e74144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245448} {:answer/id #uuid "895bf8ee-e4c3-5f21-bf0e-f9b3ae0074cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245516} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa964dc-9179-51e3-96fa-9c7480654cae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245528} {:answer/id #uuid "b0fa781a-721b-5d87-a7b6-ea511b62e328" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "808b95f4-e21b-5dd6-9146-9f4276e74144" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245448} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ae30100-63e7-5d16-9724-0a2111bb732e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d16ade3b-ac3a-55c8-a501-f72a3071e370" :question/math-academy-id "q-110307" :question/problem "The following table gives the values of $f(x),{f}^{′}(x),g(x),$ and ${g}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find ${(g\\cdot {f}^{-1})}^{′}(4)$  of the product of functions.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n| $-3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $-2$ | $-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nUsing this, and the product rule, the derivative of the function $g(x){f}^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n(g\\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(x)={g}^{′}(x){f}^{-1}(x)+\\frac{g(x)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n(g\\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(4)={g}^{′}(4){f}^{-1}(4)+\\frac{g(4)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(4)=-3,$ $g(4)=3,$ ${g}^{′}(4)=1,$ and ${f}^{′}(-3)=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g\\cdot {f}^{-1})^{′}(4) & ={g}^{′}(4){f}^{-1}(4)+\\frac{g(4)}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)+\\frac{3}{{f}^{′}(-3)} \\\\  & =-3+\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "900dcaf8-da39-5654-96cd-6aec89e379c9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Joint Probabilities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1462fb6e-9013-5d11-a121-fb769d942861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244502} {:answer/id #uuid "35e56a32-bc7c-5329-8e75-02f488f77f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244791} {:answer/id #uuid "5afd1178-ffac-5057-8d8e-90513bd72136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245109} {:answer/id #uuid "6768d1cf-2410-5169-85b8-b49d1e1140b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Impossible to determine using the given information." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245223} {:answer/id #uuid "94942d9f-5e30-5d26-ab89-0fe5cf8eae12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5afd1178-ffac-5057-8d8e-90513bd72136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245109} :answer-field/id #uuid "8406085c-4b27-5e57-9c99-c0537f607061" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3006b2b-d3f6-5ddf-b811-934181f67f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-110385" :question/problem "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(3,1).$\n\n| | $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | |  | | $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.75$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |  |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.25$ | $0.75$ |  |" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,1) & ={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.125.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064254 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Derivative Using Properties of Inverse Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16b1a423-0501-5b39-af51-063a1449f36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(9)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244525} {:answer/id #uuid "4f569904-ef32-58ac-830a-770cbc7a0c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245021} {:answer/id #uuid "6a15afd0-9e43-5b63-99bb-4dbc1112487f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245253} {:answer/id #uuid "7e112348-79c5-59f1-a699-cdfbf09ce664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245426} {:answer/id #uuid "a253b89c-a0b4-54dd-8bb0-9af5e56fc29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a253b89c-a0b4-54dd-8bb0-9af5e56fc29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245764} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e9c3b30-545f-5647-8247-656eb61ce05f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246623}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7795bda-c6a8-5a8d-b370-7dbf2eb2ee80" :question/math-academy-id "q-110497" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={3}^{x}-1.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(8).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(8),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(8)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(8))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(8).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(8)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(8) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =8 \\\\ {3}^{x}-1 & =8 \\\\ {3}^{x} & =9 \\\\ {3}^{x} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(8)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={3}^{x}-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =9\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(8) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(8))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "248c560a-5504-5344-ba06-31ff881f4228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡(2)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244640} {:answer/id #uuid "453ad4e8-fc91-5dc6-a9a5-3321c0d9dc49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡(2)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244926} {:answer/id #uuid "a51377ae-5388-50fe-83c3-7ef69418daf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2ln⁡(2)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245796} {:answer/id #uuid "f8312b64-ab69-53ae-90e8-b700b7b53c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2ln⁡(2)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246497} {:answer/id #uuid "faecbb4c-e0f8-59a8-a3d7-92a5f5e02711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2ln⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a51377ae-5388-50fe-83c3-7ef69418daf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2ln⁡(2)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245796} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a081fae-877e-5e2e-acae-a2b3a4e290d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48d44085-8aaf-5ed5-9d45-53625f178071" :question/math-academy-id "q-110536" :question/problem "Given that ${e}^{y+1}-1=3,$ then $y=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y+1}-1 & =3 \\\\ {e}^{y+1} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y+1} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{y+1}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ y+1 & =2ln⁡(2) \\\\ y & =2ln⁡(2)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=2ln⁡(2)-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8eebff2-97ca-599b-a819-04ff34f0c1c4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Exponential Equations Containing Different Bases by Rewriting Two Exponents"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5590a848-eae9-5089-bdc1-7f789ac62064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245065} {:answer/id #uuid "5f338793-8672-5f89-9124-424dc680305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245150} {:answer/id #uuid "a0029015-9d7a-5b76-8132-425f8e5b1369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245736} {:answer/id #uuid "caf954cd-bb67-553d-8e8c-ae5436312352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246122} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f19e3a-8e8b-5a89-b39e-a28325288d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246459}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5590a848-eae9-5089-bdc1-7f789ac62064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245065} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d24b5a0-aff5-5beb-bda9-0451317c58e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b4f9a18-294f-593c-86d1-c0d405dcd6de" :question/math-academy-id "q-110544" :question/problem "Solve for $y$ where ${81}^{y}={27}^{y+5}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this equation, we need both exponential terms to have a common base. To do this, we rewrite the equation using $81={3}^{4}$ and $27={3}^{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{({3}^{4})}^{y}={({3}^{3})}^{y+5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule of exponents. This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4y}={3}^{3(y+5)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(3),$ we equate the exponents and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y & =3(y+5) \\\\ 4y & =3y+15 \\\\ y & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064366 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ee8a3a-aff1-5329-ab62-d486c9340be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244398} {:answer/id #uuid "89609260-8cd9-5ba1-b619-2fc1bd29c3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245517} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8724d8-cb92-559c-84a5-0132b5fbd151" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245551} {:answer/id #uuid "962ee919-f8a1-5686-b7b2-8aaf7083525a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245636} {:answer/id #uuid "d758ea7b-694a-526b-a30b-4e618f038f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ee8a3a-aff1-5329-ab62-d486c9340be5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244398} :answer-field/id #uuid "5935a167-843e-514d-9aca-7a9d8403bae1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8030974-10cb-5204-836f-a9b8dc5afc64" :question/math-academy-id "q-110625" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=5x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x+4\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =5+4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =5+4(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =5-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064366 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14063917-2f5c-53ac-a1be-a84525cdd48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244495} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbb79dc-d168-5e6c-967d-301ffb7b9bec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244839} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0b8241-b7f9-55f9-8dd0-032a83734e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245852} {:answer/id #uuid "c978eae8-643b-508b-8afb-0d9a95c8c8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246098} {:answer/id #uuid "caebc49d-d3db-5490-82b2-efb3f04c7f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+\\frac{15x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c978eae8-643b-508b-8afb-0d9a95c8c8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246098} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf16ad5d-42c4-5764-9634-f695fe575fed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7680792c-1905-5073-9b89-1803e3b68661" :question/math-academy-id "q-110626" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=15\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+8x.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(15\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x+8x) \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)+8 \\\\  & =15(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})+8 \\\\  & =8-\\frac{15}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064367 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "149dcaee-a842-584c-9fc7-09c4da3304aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6{x}^{2}+3{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244503} {:answer/id #uuid "768d48e2-8c95-5280-ba0c-8ed707947487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}-6{x}^{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245367} {:answer/id #uuid "80e24ca9-2891-539c-a111-b07fb4ce033f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{3}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245451} {:answer/id #uuid "8759d4f9-38b4-5c69-b25c-92f362595b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245505} {:answer/id #uuid "ef4377e7-ae39-50b4-a1fe-882b741bc63b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}+{x}^{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8759d4f9-38b4-5c69-b25c-92f362595b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245505} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b18822-cc1c-50af-9989-8e193167758f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2888c71d-c895-59c2-afdb-577636636ba4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110762" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{{x}^{6}+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{{x}^{6}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6}+1)}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot 6{x}^{5}}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{({x}^{6}+1)(3{x}^{2})}{{x}^{6}+1}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡({x}^{3})}{({x}^{6}+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064367 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22a2e63d-ce23-5f94-b43c-fe498a90aeef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244617} {:answer/id #uuid "5d4c6d81-2c16-5cd7-b161-403eb27b5d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245137} {:answer/id #uuid "646d492b-7b50-5a66-b9d1-b587fee404cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245197} {:answer/id #uuid "aca6fa25-92b4-55d1-9de0-7256742207ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245855} {:answer/id #uuid "f3bf57b6-e50e-5557-a8b2-a49cf3d68351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}+\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d4c6d81-2c16-5cd7-b161-403eb27b5d97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245137} :answer-field/id #uuid "1df422f0-6fd5-5d06-9f9a-8e3773d8232b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246598}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fce053b7-4dd3-554f-bea5-f458f557cfe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-110777" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the quotient rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$  we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})}{{({e}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157437 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3758cf02-ba4b-539a-bc61-8c2030ff6f6f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation by Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "745439dc-de09-51c8-bbdb-eedea4d0f155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386573} {:answer/id #uuid "617f1c2d-99ac-5b8a-931f-683ccf1893b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386574} {:answer/id #uuid "db8e533b-8461-5017-a4f6-47771a90f0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386575} {:answer/id #uuid "e510aa7f-7425-5853-824c-91e79e70849b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386576} {:answer/id #uuid "2d786935-adc1-5afa-a4cc-25f126fdd263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e510aa7f-7425-5853-824c-91e79e70849b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386576} :answer-field/id #uuid "50a99769-405d-5ab0-ad5f-e1bf8543c410" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "11afc858-764d-5d9d-a321-3ddf5528f806" :question/math-academy-id "q-110801" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{2-x}-{7}^{2-x}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {7}^{2-x}-{7}^{2-x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-1)\\cdot {7}^{2-x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-1=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{7}^{2-x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-1=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-1)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-1,1.$\n\n- The equation ${7}^{2-x}=0$ has no solutions because ${7}^{2-x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-1,1,$ and their product is $-1\\cdot 1=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386578 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157438 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aaf12cf-8596-5960-bc68-5ca3eb5fab0f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Equation by Rearranging the Equation and Then Factoring"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83cca658-4075-5016-8fbe-e5612324db1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386580} {:answer/id #uuid "bb580306-8e14-5c41-83ea-3c1ee2e8cdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386581} {:answer/id #uuid "c11a3bed-2998-59a1-97a6-f48556210e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386582} {:answer/id #uuid "e3957c19-6d34-5546-aa5e-4ed5649688c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386583} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddd09f0-bf49-52e2-98a4-7a4a058d7c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3957c19-6d34-5546-aa5e-4ed5649688c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386583} :answer-field/id #uuid "e20ce4da-f186-5091-a95d-1d090861a47d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ddd6b32-1ad1-5a92-b6ca-5f243dfcc079" :question/math-academy-id "q-110803" :question/problem "What is the product of solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}{10}^{2-x}={10}^{2-x}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{10}^{2-x} & ={10}^{2-x} \\\\ {x}^{2}{10}^{2-x}-{10}^{2-x} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-1){10}^{2-x} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-1=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{10}^{2-x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}-1=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-1)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-1,1.$\n\n- The equation ${10}^{2-x}=0$ has no solutions because ${10}^{2-x}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, the original equation has the solutions $x=-1,1,$ and their product is $(-1)\\cdot 1=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115399 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20a5f15e-8a26-57af-a867-8f8ae02a91c1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6a9bcf-5b72-54d9-a128-8bd6ee36de0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244573} {:answer/id #uuid "3a12daab-bb88-55ce-a334-ad69cb782225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{arccscx}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244829} {:answer/id #uuid "734eb1e5-5d2c-548c-a909-d144450435b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x+2}{arcsecx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245345} {:answer/id #uuid "d5f3b612-bac7-5a34-a41e-8ffc73c0c464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246219} {:answer/id #uuid "f484b6c9-af99-5523-b72f-2c18bf53b1b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}+4}{arccscx}-\\frac{2x+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5f3b612-bac7-5a34-a41e-8ffc73c0c464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246219} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a0c5df-079e-53e1-9ee0-47a76e0ae5a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246987}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "698df1fd-5fd3-5825-8b74-4170ba6ffbf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-110834" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{arccscx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we let $u(x)={x}^{2}+4x$ and $v(x)=arccscx,$ and apply the quotient rule.\n\nWe use the formulae\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x+4\\,\\text{and}\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+4)\\cdot arccscx-({x}^{2}+4x)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}})}{{arccsc}^{2}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+4}{arccscx}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\cdot {arccsc}^{2}x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f601647-230e-5af7-8fdc-0bae52efde5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244454} {:answer/id #uuid "98e4c4ad-77ea-5c87-8eff-67bc80e8c7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245669} {:answer/id #uuid "9c00972e-c8f8-54a5-bef4-34dd5a3d7982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245695} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc6aa1d-3ce4-569f-8f6e-e796f0e81b07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246148} {:answer/id #uuid "f1701159-5573-5c32-8131-e7a9c983e05f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246445}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98e4c4ad-77ea-5c87-8eff-67bc80e8c7a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245669} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f03617f-944d-54be-95dd-7bce058bae74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6466b906-2338-59f9-b490-f79a50950cf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-111032" :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,2),(2,3)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,3)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f3ba5d-e75a-5ecf-a19b-64923cce981a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244362} {:answer/id #uuid "36d0ef4c-2791-5c6a-99b9-b1aa2cd23e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244799} {:answer/id #uuid "56d4fc95-c564-5a8f-9fcb-d46a1dc55b28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245078} {:answer/id #uuid "6e279fce-d7a1-5c40-980d-2c4ae52392d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245288} {:answer/id #uuid "79f2e7bf-b778-5573-890d-9c522914975b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e279fce-d7a1-5c40-980d-2c4ae52392d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5767537-bf21-5ec8-a24b-cbcf91edba98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed526ede-6ba9-5979-b07c-e565cdc8a6e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-111076" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=4\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,5),(4,1),(4,3),(4,5)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,5))+P((X,Y)=(4,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(4,3))+P((X,Y)=(4,5)) \\\\  & =f(2,5)+f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162074 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200116a5-7902-57a3-9fa2-4f03f4d87f01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244597} {:answer/id #uuid "39161e73-e6f0-5b4e-ab1a-792746c51920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244820} {:answer/id #uuid "498c817c-3fcd-58db-b2ef-6442d4ed2e09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244969} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d9fb4c-1223-5390-99ef-97e58115bc96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245831} {:answer/id #uuid "aeff8a81-5e38-5faf-8225-cc84b232511c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeff8a81-5e38-5faf-8225-cc84b232511c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245875} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8644d15-eeb4-52d5-8fd7-da4e9ded447b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0172d82e-e716-5982-89be-170e2ffe9720" :question/math-academy-id "q-111083" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,1),(1,1),(1,2),(2,1)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.25+0.1+0.25 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176004 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8995cd9c-994e-54e6-8213-f832e7dbf978" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Distributions of Squared Random Variables: One-to-One Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d1aa619-6cc5-5d75-b134-af72b193895b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398028} {:answer/id #uuid "a34e4842-6531-564e-a6a6-c96f33ae44d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398029} {:answer/id #uuid "82bc5a36-0c04-528c-890e-b56ee17134b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398030} {:answer/id #uuid "16c68d94-9b05-57c8-9365-8d1bcf39811d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398031} {:answer/id #uuid "003fd3e7-d9ba-5c66-bdc0-bf0b319a14ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398032}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a34e4842-6531-564e-a6a6-c96f33ae44d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398029} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ca4f5be-e68b-52cd-a172-bc29c42f3800" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62e4eef6-5308-5ab7-84b8-bf11a12097d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-111309" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=3{X}^{3}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $0$ | $b$ | $24$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $0.2$ | $d$ | $0.3$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $b+d?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=3{X}^{3}$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ | $24$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $3$ | $24$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, $b=3,$ $d=0.4,$ and $b+d=3.4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398033 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176004 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8995cd9c-994e-54e6-8213-f832e7dbf978" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Distributions of Squared Random Variables: One-to-One Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "467c04af-80d7-599d-8f1c-7b916454d808" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398035} {:answer/id #uuid "b9caa425-46ca-5c2d-9317-f7c935d02abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398036} {:answer/id #uuid "00d94389-de94-5c74-9e85-dd25e84d954c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398037} {:answer/id #uuid "58cf5293-65e5-57ca-84cd-edef12644219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398038} {:answer/id #uuid "1b33daec-6d8c-5621-ad0d-3034be2f4c26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58cf5293-65e5-57ca-84cd-edef12644219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398038} :answer-field/id #uuid "3669273d-479a-574a-b298-e4163093531f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d551bbb5-65f5-5733-b15c-2c116cdaa662" :question/math-academy-id "q-111311" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=5-{X}^{3}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $a$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $b$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y=5-{X}^{3}$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.55$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.55$ | $0.25$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $c=0.2,$ and $a+c=6.2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176005 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f31f7959-b99f-587a-bec3-374e437a2706" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Distributions of Squared Random Variables: Many-to-One Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87e5ba5a-5