r/value "17.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04b0d72c-5108-5fbf-ace0-f2715e5c96cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398043} :answer-field/id #uuid "0572a59f-f626-587d-9b91-48cabe6f883d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398040}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2568364-334f-50f4-8bf6-71938e74b4ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-111314" :question/problem "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\nLet $Y={X}^{4}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $a$ | $b$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $0.2$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+b+d?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's add a $Y={X}^{4}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $16$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.5$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in {0,1,16}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for both $Y=1$ and $Y=16.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.2 \\\\ P(Y=1) & =0.1+0.1 \\\\ P(Y=16) & =0.1+0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.2$ | $0.6$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=1,b=16,d=0.6,$ and $a+b+d=17.6.$"}]}
